  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.3.0 - Azure event type\n- Adds LogAzureEvent and LogAzureEventBuilder for Azure Monitor records streamed\n  through Event Hubs (subscription, resource group, resource, category, operation,\n  result, caller, properties). ToLog() sets _sys_type=azure and azure.* attributes.\n- Level parsing accepts Azure's \"Informational\" and \"Verbose\".\n- No breaking API changes\n\nv5.2.0 - Kubernetes event type\n- Adds LogKubernetesEvent and LogKubernetesEventBuilder for pod container logs\n  (namespace, pod, uid, container, image, node, stream, restart count, owner,\n  labels, annotations). ToLog() sets _sys_type=kubernetes and k8s.* attributes\n  for server-side routing.\n- No breaking API changes\n\nv5.1.6 - Packaging fix: include the quiet-ApiKey-fallback change\n- The \"stop warning when filling Log.ApiKey from options\" change landed after the\n  5.1.5 tag was cut, so published 5.1.5 still emitted \"ApiKey was missing on log\n  in batch, set from options\" on every batch send. 5.1.6 ships from the branch\n  that includes it, so the benign warning is gone.\n- Also carries the 5.1.5 server-rejection-reason logging and public SetUserId.\n- No API changes\n\nv5.1.5 - Surface server rejection reasons\n- When the server declines a record, NativeProtocolClient now logs the server's\n  reason (\"Server rejected record: ...\") instead of silently collapsing every\n  non-Success status to a bare Failed enum - client consoles can show WHY a\n  send failed, not just that it did\n- No API changes\n\nv5.1.4 - Quiet ApiKey fallback + Public SetUserId\n- LogDBClient no longer warns when filling Log.ApiKey from options on the batch path.\n- Log.ApiKey is internal by design; the fallback is the intended code path, not a misuse.\n- Exposes LogEventBuilder.SetUserId as public so callers can attach a user id to log events\n- No breaking API changes\n\nv5.1.1 - NuGet.org Release\n- Publishes the public package line to nuget.org for unauthenticated consumption\n- Keeps the AutoMapper-free client package as the active public release line\n- No breaking API changes\n\nv5.0.18 - Version Line Alignment\n- Aligns LogDB.Client version with current public 5.0.18 release train\n- Keeps metadata in sync with SDK integrations and docs\n- No breaking API changes\n\nv5.0.0 - Standalone Package\n- BREAKING: Package is now fully standalone with no external dependencies on LogDB.Shared\n- All models are now defined within the package\n- Clean public API surface - internal implementation details hidden\n- Ready for open source distribution\n- Maintains full backward compatibility for public APIs\n\nv4.0.10 - Previous Release\n- Bug fixes and stability improvements",
